**Given:**

Length of the rectangular field = dfrac{2a+2sqrt{5}}{4} m

Breadth of the rectangular field = dfrac{a-sqrt{5}}{2} m

**Formula used:**

Area of a rectangle = Length × Breadth

**Calculation:**

Area = dfrac{2a+2sqrt{5}}{4} times dfrac{a-sqrt{5}}{2}

⇒ Area = dfrac{(2a+2sqrt{5})(a-sqrt{5})}{4 times 2}

⇒ Area = dfrac{(2a · a + 2a · -sqrt{5} + 2sqrt{5} · a + 2sqrt{5} · -sqrt{5})}{8}

⇒ Area = dfrac{(2a² - 2asqrt{5} + 2asqrt{5} - 10)}{8}

⇒ Area = dfrac{2a² - 10}{8}

⇒ Area = ((a² - 5)/(4))m².

**∴ The correct answer is option (1).**
